STYLE: A grand hand-made toy theatre production built from printed card. Every piece is a flat cutout of thick card about 4 mm thick, cut by hand with a craft knife, with raw brown card at the edges. The face is painted in soft charcoal line and grey ink wash with thin watercolour on warm Korean hanji mulberry paper, its long fibres visible. Loose expressive charcoal strokes and quiet, tender faces. Broad, calm shapes readable from the back row. Puppet joints are round brass split pins. Korea, many years after a war divided two brothers: the older one's near bank has concrete embankments, metal railings, streetlights and densely built apartment blocks; the far bank has sparse, worn rural houses, fields, dirt roads and a few dim lights. The river and the closed crossing still divide them. The present is dusk amber against indigo; the June 1950 memory is cold rain, refugees and opposing troops. Palette: hanji cream #EDE6D6, charcoal #2B2A28, slate #5E6670, mist #C9CDD0, earth #6E5A44, indigo #3B4A66, pine #4E5E48, persimmon #B4553A, dusk amber #D6A365, raw card #A57E52. Muted olive and mustard khaki distinguish the wartime uniforms; plain blue and plain red cloth banners carry no marks. Family love and the lasting wound of war, with equal humanity on both banks.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, writing, lettering, numbers, country names, logos, signature or watermark. No national flags, insignia, emblems, armbands or badges. Plain unmarked red or blue cloth banners are allowed in the war memory. Rifles remain slung and no weapon is fired. No gore or graphic violence. No real persons. No photographic people, plastic, glossy finish, anime style or sculpted 3D characters. Everything remains painted flat card. No triumphant propaganda or caricatures. Rods, strings, light and sky are supplied by the theatre.
Use case: illustration-story.
Image 1 is the revised key-art style and geography reference. One long foreground scenery cutout of the developed near-bank observation embankment: a low straight strip of grey concrete paving and retaining wall, a simple steel handrail running along the river edge, one tall slender working streetlamp near the LEFT fifth, and at the RIGHT end a CLOSED unmarked chain-link access gate with a short fence, barring the approach to an old crossing. The gate remains closed. The railing is simple and open, with clear gaps; the streetlamp and gate must be fully in frame. The card must let a puppet behind it remain visible from the waist up. No road sign, writing, logo or people. Contemporary infrastructure painted in the same soft charcoal, ink and watercolour on textured hanji, not photo-real metal. A wide landscape cutout. One single front-facing flat cardboard scenery cutout on a genuinely transparent alpha background. Clear empty margin. No background wash, sky, water, shadows, lettering, frame, rods or strings. The bottom edge is straight. The top follows the actual silhouette, with every gap transparent.
EDIT THE ATTACHED IMAGE INTO A STAGE CUTOUT. Keep ONLY the foreground concrete paving strip, the near steel railing, the single tall lamp at the left, and the padlocked chain-link gate at the right. Erase ALL distant apartment blocks, trees, mountains, rural houses, watchtower, bridges, skyline, river and reflections. The entire region behind and above the foreground railing must be genuinely transparent alpha, including the open gaps between rail bars. Only the lamp may rise high above the railing. There must be NO background scene whatsoever. The previous image wrongly included the background; this edit is expressly to remove it. Preserve the paint and layout of those foreground items exactly. Transparent background.
